{
    "cells": [
        {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Critical stimulus"]},
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 2,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "import immunowave as iw\n",
                "import diffrax as dx\n",
                "import equinox as eqx\n",
                "import jax\n",
                "import jax.numpy as jnp\n",
                "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
                "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                "import math\n",
                "\n",
                'jax.config.update("jax_enable_x64", True)',
            ],
        },
        {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### Define model"]},
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Our state is only $u(\\mathbf{x},t)$"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 3,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": ["class State(iw.State):\n", "    u: iw.ScalarField"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Our dynamical variable $u$ satisfies\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\\partial_t u = \\nabla^2 u + f(u) + 2 I \\delta\n",
                "$$\n",
                "\n",
                "where\n",
                "$$\n",
                "f(u) = \\frac{u^n}{K^n + u^n} - u\n",
                "$$\n",
                "with $I, K > 0$, and $n > 1$.",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 4,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "class Model(iw.Model):\n",
                "    K: float\n",
                "    n: float\n",
                "    I: float\n",
                "    # Bandwidth adjustment for Dirac delta approximation (grid units)\n",
                "    bw_adjust: float = 2.0\n",
                "\n",
                "    def f(self, u):\n",
                "        K, n = self.K, self.n\n",
                "        return u.hill(K, n) - u\n",
                "\n",
                "    def delta(self, u):\n",
                '        """Helper function to approximate a Dirac delta as a Gaussian on the same grid as u."""\n',
                "        σ = self.bw_adjust * u.h\n",
                "\n",
                "        def gaussian(*coords):\n",
                "            squared_dist = sum(coord**2 for coord in coords)\n",
                "            return jnp.exp(-squared_dist / (2 * σ**2))\n",
                "\n",
                "        result = iw.ScalarField(u.values.shape, u.lb, u.h, fn=gaussian)\n",
                "        result /= result.integral()\n",
                "        return result\n",
                "\n",
                "    def __call__(self, t, state: State, args=None):\n",
                "        u = state.u\n",
                '        Δu = u.laplacian(bc="neumann")\n',
                "        f = self.f\n",
                "        I = self.I\n",
                "        δ = self.delta(u)\n",
                "\n",
                "        dudt = Δu + f(u) + 2 * I * δ\n",
                "\n",
                "        return State(dudt)",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Analytical $I_c$\n",
                "\n",
                "For $K\\ll1$, the unstable fixed point is approximately $u_1 \\approx K^{n/(n-1)}$, and the critical stimulus is\n",
                "$$\n",
                "I_c \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{n-1}{n+1}}\\,u_1\n",
                "$$\n",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 5,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "def u1(K, n):\n",
                "    return K ** (n / (n - 1))\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "def Ic(K, n):\n",
                "    return ((n - 1) / (n + 1)) ** 0.5 * u1(K, n)",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Set reference parameters"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 6,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": ["K = 0.01\n", "n = 2.0"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 7,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {"text/plain": ["(0.0001, 5.773502691896258e-05)"]},
                    "execution_count": 7,
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "execute_result",
                }
            ],
            "source": ["u1(K, n), Ic(K, n)"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Plot the Hill function $f(u)$ and the line $u$."],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 8,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stderr",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "WARNING:2025-07-28 14:33:22,447:jax._src.xla_bridge:872: An NVIDIA GPU may be present on this machine, but a CUDA-enabled jaxlib is not installed. Falling back to cpu.\n"
                    ],
                },
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": "",
                        "text/plain": ["<Figure size 400x300 with 1 Axes>"],
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                },
            ],
            "source": [
                "u_grid = jnp.linspace(0, 2 * u1(K, n), 100)\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(4, 3))\n",
                'plt.plot(u_grid, u_grid**n / (K**n + u_grid**n), label=r"$\\frac{u^n}{K^n + u^n}$")\n',
                'plt.plot(u_grid, u_grid, label=r"$u$")\n',
                'plt.axvline(u1(K, n), color="k", linestyle="--", label=r"$u_1\\approx K^\\frac{n}{n-1}$")\n',
                'plt.xlabel("u")\n',
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()",
            ],
        },
        {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### Initialize fields"]},
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Spatial discretization, initialized to zero."],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 9,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "L = 20.0\n",
                "lb = [-L / 2]\n",
                "n_spatial = 200\n",
                "shape = (n_spatial,)\n",
                "h = L / (n_spatial - 1)\n",
                "\n",
                "state = State(u=iw.ScalarField(shape, lb, h, 0))",
            ],
        },
        {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## Solve"]},
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Define the integration region as $t\\ge 0$, and solve until steady state, taking only the final time only.\n",
                "We will define a custom norm to identify the steady state via the spatial region within distance $L/4$ from the origin (avoiding boundary effects).",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 10,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "t0 = 0.0\n",
                "t1 = jnp.inf\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "@jax.jit\n",
                "def norm(state: State):\n",
                "    d = state.u.ndim\n",
                "    L = state.u.ub[0] - state.u.lb[0]  # Length of the domain in first dimension\n",
                "    # indicator function for middle of the domain\n",
                "    ind = iw.ScalarField(\n",
                "        state.u.values.shape,\n",
                "        state.u.lb,\n",
                "        state.u.h,\n",
                "        fn=lambda *coords: jnp.where(\n",
                "            sum(abs(coord) ** d for coord in coords) ** (1 / d) < L / 4, 1.0, 0.0\n",
                "        ),\n",
                "    )\n",
                "    return (ind * state.u).integral() / ind.integral()\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "steady_state_event = dx.Event(dx.steady_state_event(atol=0, rtol=1e-3, norm=norm))",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Keyword arguments for the solver"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 11,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "kwargs = dict(\n",
                "    dt0=1e-4,\n",
                "    max_steps=10000000,\n",
                "    atol=1e-8,\n",
                "    rtol=1e-8,\n",
                "    throw=True,\n",
                "    event=steady_state_event,\n",
                ")",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["### Mean activation at steady state"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 12,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "@jax.jit\n",
                "def mean_activation(model, state):\n",
                "    steady_state = iw.solve(model, state, 0, jnp.inf, **kwargs).ys.u.map(jnp.squeeze)\n",
                "    area = math.prod(ub - lb for ub, lb in zip(state.u.ub, state.u.lb))\n",
                "    return steady_state.integral() / area",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Solve over a grid of $I$ values, and plot the mean activation at steady state."
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 13,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": "",
                        "text/plain": ["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "I_grid = jnp.geomspace(0.1 * Ic(K, n), 10 * Ic(K, n), 50)\n",
                "models = [Model(K=K, n=n, I=I) for I in I_grid]\n",
                "\n",
                'plt.plot(I_grid, [mean_activation(model, state) for model in models], ".")\n',
                "plt.axvline(\n",
                "    Ic(K, n),\n",
                '    color="k",\n',
                '    linestyle="--",\n',
                '    label=r"$I_c \\approx \\frac{n-1}{n+1}\\,K^\\frac{n}{n-1}$",\n',
                ")\n",
                "plt.legend()\n",
                'plt.xlabel("I")\n',
                'plt.ylabel(r"$\\frac{1}{L} \\int u(x, \\infty) \\, \\mathrm{d}x$")\n',
                'plt.xscale("log")\n',
                "plt.show()",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Bisection algorithm for $I_c$\n",
                "\n",
                "Define a function to perform a bisection algorithm to find the critical stimulus $I_c$.\n",
                "The idea is to bound from below and above the critical stimulus, and then solve the steady state for the midpoint of the bounding interval.\n",
                "If the midpoint results in an activated steady state, the midpoint becomes the new upper bound, otherwise it becomes the new lower bound.\n",
                "The bounding interval is thus reduced by half at each iteration.",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 14,
            "metadata": {"vscode": {"languageId": "ruby"}},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "def find_Ic(model, state, tolerance=1e-3, max_iterations=20, verbose=False):\n",
                "    _print = print if verbose else lambda *args, **kwargs: None\n",
                "    # initial bounds\n",
                "    model_low = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model, 0.9 * model.I)\n",
                "    model_high = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model, 1.1 * model.I)\n",
                "    # If low bound doesn't give low activation, reduce it\n",
                "    while mean_activation(model_low, state) > 0.5:\n",
                '        _print("decreasing invalid lower bound")\n',
                "        model_low = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model_low, model_low.I / 2)\n",
                "    # If high bound doesn't give high activation, increase it\n",
                "    while mean_activation(model_high, state) < 0.5:\n",
                '        _print("increasing invalid upper bound")\n',
                "        model_high = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model_high, 2 * model_high.I)\n",
                "\n",
                "    # Iteratively bisect bounding interval\n",
                "    for i in range(max_iterations):\n",
                '        _print(f"iter {i}: [{model_low.I:.3e}, {model_high.I:.3e}]")\n',
                "        model_mid = eqx.tree_at(\n",
                "            lambda m: m.I, model_low, (model_low.I + model_high.I) / 2\n",
                "        )\n",
                "        if (model_high.I - model_low.I) / model_mid.I < tolerance:\n",
                '            _print(f"tolerance satisifed: Ic = {model_mid.I:.3e}")\n',
                "            return model_mid\n",
                "        if mean_activation(model_mid, state) < 0.5:\n",
                "            model_low = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model, model_mid.I)\n",
                "        else:\n",
                "            model_high = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.I, model, model_mid.I)\n",
                "\n",
                '    raise RuntimeError("max iterations reached")\n',
                "    return model_mid",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Find the critical stimulus $I_c$ numerically for the reference model, and compare with the theoretical value."
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 15,
            "metadata": {"vscode": {"languageId": "ruby"}},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "text/plain": ["Model(K=0.01, n=2.0, I=5.773502691896258e-05)"]
                    },
                    "execution_count": 15,
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "execute_result",
                }
            ],
            "source": ["model = Model(K=K, n=n, I=Ic(K, n))\n", "model"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 16,
            "metadata": {"vscode": {"languageId": "ruby"}},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "iter 0: [5.196e-05, 6.351e-05]\n",
                        "iter 1: [5.774e-05, 6.351e-05]\n",
                        "iter 2: [5.774e-05, 6.062e-05]\n",
                        "iter 3: [5.774e-05, 5.918e-05]\n",
                        "iter 4: [5.846e-05, 5.918e-05]\n",
                        "iter 5: [5.846e-05, 5.882e-05]\n",
                        "iter 6: [5.864e-05, 5.882e-05]\n",
                        "iter 7: [5.873e-05, 5.882e-05]\n",
                        "iter 8: [5.877e-05, 5.882e-05]\n",
                        "tolerance satisifed: Ic = 5.880e-05\n",
                        "\n",
                        "theoretical Ic = 5.774e-05\n",
                    ],
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "find_Ic(model, state, verbose=True)\n",
                'print(f"\\ntheoretical Ic = {Ic(K, n):.3e}")',
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "Find the critical stimulus $I_c$ numerically over a grid of $K$, and compare with the theoretical values."
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 17,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": "",
                        "text/plain": ["<Figure size 300x300 with 1 Axes>"],
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                },
                {
                    "data": {
                        "text/plain": [
                            "Array([1.01835938, 1.01835938, 1.01835937, 1.01835937, 1.01835937,\n",
                            "       1.01835937, 1.01835938, 1.01835937, 1.01835938, 1.01835938,\n",
                            "       1.01835938, 1.01914063, 1.01914063, 1.01914063, 1.01992187,\n",
                            "       1.01992187, 1.02070313, 1.02148438, 1.02226562, 1.02382813],      dtype=float64)",
                        ]
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                },
            ],
            "source": [
                "def K_sweep(state):\n",
                "    K_grid = jnp.geomspace(0.01, 0.1, 20)\n",
                "    models = [Model(K=K, n=n, I=Ic(K, n)) for K in K_grid]\n",
                "    Ic_grid = jnp.array([find_Ic(model, state).I for model in models])\n",
                "\n",
                "    plt.figure(figsize=(3, 3))\n",
                '    plt.plot(K_grid, Ic(K_grid, n), "-", label="analytical")\n',
                '    plt.plot(K_grid, Ic_grid, "ko", label="numerical", fillstyle="none")\n',
                '    plt.xscale("log")\n',
                '    plt.yscale("log")\n',
                '    plt.xlabel("K")\n',
                '    plt.ylabel(r"$I_c$")\n',
                "    plt.legend()\n",
                "    plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "    display(Ic_grid / Ic(K_grid, n))\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "K_sweep(state)",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["Similarly, over a grid of $n$."],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 18,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": "",
                        "text/plain": ["<Figure size 300x300 with 1 Axes>"],
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                },
                {
                    "data": {
                        "text/plain": [
                            "Array([1.00898438, 1.01132812, 1.01367188, 1.01601563, 1.01914063,\n",
                            "       1.02148438, 1.02382813, 1.02695313, 1.02929688, 1.03085938,\n",
                            "       1.03320312, 1.03554688, 1.03710938, 1.03945313, 1.04101562,\n",
                            "       1.04257812, 1.04414063, 1.04648438, 1.04804688, 1.04960937],      dtype=float64)",
                        ]
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data",
                },
            ],
            "source": [
                "def n_sweep(state):\n",
                "    n_grid = jnp.linspace(1.3, 5.0, 20)\n",
                "    models = [Model(K=K, n=n, I=Ic(K, n)) for n in n_grid]\n",
                "    Ic_grid = jnp.array([find_Ic(model, state).I for model in models])\n",
                "\n",
                "    plt.figure(figsize=(3, 3))\n",
                '    plt.plot(n_grid, Ic(K, n_grid), "-", label="analytical")\n',
                '    plt.plot(n_grid, Ic_grid, "ko", label="numerical", fillstyle="none")\n',
                '    plt.yscale("log")\n',
                '    plt.xlabel("n")\n',
                '    plt.ylabel(r"$I_c$")\n',
                "    plt.xlim(1, None)\n",
                "    plt.legend()\n",
                "    plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "    display(Ic_grid / Ic(K, n_grid))\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "n_sweep(state)",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2D\n",
                "\n",
                "Now we can reap the rewards of code abstraction, and rerun the above with a 2D spatial domain.",
            ],
